naming conventions, and architecture visible in the files below. Do not
introduce new dependencies or restructure unrelated code.

ISSUE TITLE: SMS connector: document provider abstraction boundary
ISSUE DESCRIPTION:
Parent: #34

## Problem
Shops may want SMS alerts through different providers. Posnic should define the abstraction before adding provider-specific code.

## Acceptance criteria
- [ ] Document common SMS provider inputs: destination, template/message, sender id, status callback, and cost/error metadata.
- [ ] Define privacy and opt-in boundaries for customer phone numbers.
- [ ] Propose a fake SMS provider fixture for tests.
- [ ] State that no real SMS is sent by default.

## Out of scope
- Integrating a specific SMS provider.
- Marketing automation.

ISSUE LABELS: documentation, good first issue, help wanted, area: integrations, needs evidence, size: small, community edition, security
DOMAIN: this issue lives in the docs area -- respect that layer's conventions (e.g. typed API surfaces, framework idioms, model/data contracts) and do not leak concerns across layers.


RELEVANT FILES:
